6. Trained dictionaries
   mzip_dicts.h and train_corpus/*.bin hold zstd dictionaries trained on files
   from public projects: README, CHANGELOG, configuration, source code and SQL
   files from about sixty GitHub repositories, including GPL-licensed ones such
   as the Linux kernel, git and OpenJDK (the list is train_corpus/fetch.sh), and,
   for dictionary 13 (train_corpus/hf_dict.bin), model-repository metadata JSON
   (config.json, tokenizer_config.json, generation_config.json,
   special_tokens_map.json) from the 120 most-downloaded Hugging Face models on
   2026-09-02; the individual repositories and their licenses were not recorded.
   A trained dictionary contains fragments of its training
   text, and those fragments stay under their sources' licenses. The
   dictionaries are scheduled to be retrained from permissively licensed,
   recorded sources only.


7. Benchmark inputs
   real_bench/ holds 50 compression-benchmark inputs. None is part of mzip and
   none is covered by this repository's Apache-2.0 license.
   - 28 are copied from public projects and keep their original copyright and
     license: MIT, BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0 (one with the LLVM exception, one
     with the Swift runtime exception), MIT OR Apache-2.0, GPL-2.0-only (two
     Linux kernel files), GPL-2.0-only with the Classpath exception (OpenJDK),
     EPL-1.0, CC-BY-SA-3.0 and CC0-1.0.
   - 22 have no known upstream and their license is unknown; most show signs of
     having been generated for this benchmark.
   real_bench/SOURCES.md lists every file with its source, license and the
   license text in LICENSES/ that goes with it. samples/ holds synthetic data
   generated by generators.hpp.


